    "updated_at": "2026-04-13T08:36:33Z",
    "body": "I've investigated Chrome's behavior because I wanted to know why this is not showing up as a problem there (like on reddit.com, when spamming back/forward multiple times).\n\nIt appears that Chrome runs this step synchronously (i.e. the one that says \"resume apply the history steps\"). But I would need input from an actual chrome engineer to verify what I've found.\n\nHere's the execution/call stack that I think suggests it's running sync on Chrome:\n\n 1. [CommitSameDocumentNavigation()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/document_loader.cc;l=1724)\n 2. → [NavigationApi::DispatchNavigateEvent()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/navigation_api/navigation_api.cc;l=905;drc=d91b6e29a145291a28cb91f86c95dd48a8b4e41e)\n 3. → [NavigateEvent::MaybeCommitImmediately()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/navigation_api/navigate_event.cc;l=454;drc=d91b6e29a145291a28cb91f86c95dd48a8b4e41e)\n 4. → [NavigateEvent::CommitNow()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/navigation_api/navigate_event.cc;l=511;drc=d91b6e29a145291a28cb91f86c95dd48a8b4e41e)\n 5. → [RunURLAndHistoryUpdateSteps()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/document_loader.cc;l=1147;drc=d91b6e29a145291a28cb91f86c95dd48a8b4e41e)\n 6. → [NavigationApi::UpdateForNavigation()](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/navigation_api/navigation_api.cc;l=269,289,293)\n    1. → transition_->ResolveCommittedPromise()   ← .committed resolves\n    2. → DispatchEvent(currententrychange)         ← entries already updated\n    3. → FinalizeNavigationActionPromisesList()    ← intercept() handlers kicked off\n\nMaybe you could provide some insight here, @noamr ?",
